    "summary": "I built a two-bin utensil holder: two full hex cells side by side, each two storeys tall, joined with a joint bolt. Each cell holds a solid-floored bin about 160 mm deep, deep enough for utensils to stand up. All open faces have solid end caps. 19 parts, roughly 2 kg of filament. check_build passes with no rule issues and the mesh check reads clear. I couldn't show forks or spoons in the bins because the props only lie flat and won't fit lying down. I can't meet the waterproof or dishwasher-safe requirements. The configurator only checks shape and fit. Whether the holder survives water or a dishwasher depends on the material and how it's printed, and the tool can't check either.",
